🧠 Core Concepts and Domains Covered

The learning journey established a strong baseline in the following domains:

| Domain | Key Concepts Learned | Business Context / Application |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Security Architecture | OSI Model, TCP/IP, Cryptography (Symmetric vs. Asymmetric), Defense in Depth. | Understanding network flow and where security controls (Firewalls, IDS) are best implemented. |
| Vulnerability & Risk | Vulnerability vs. Exploit, Risk Management (Qualitative & Quantitative), Threat Modeling. | Ability to communicate risk to non-technical stakeholders and prioritize remediation efforts. |
| Access Control | Authentication, Authorization, Accounting (AAA), Least Privilege, Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA). | Designing secure access policies and procedures for organizational assets. |
| Governance, Risk & Compliance (GRC) | Data protection laws (e.g., GDPR), Compliance Audits, Information Security Policies. | Ensuring the security program aligns with legal, regulatory, and business requirements. |
| Operational Security | Incident Response Lifecycle, Disaster Recovery, Business Continuity Planning. | Understanding the procedures for minimizing damage and downtime following an incident. |

